  "question": {
    "text": "Which of the following are arranged in an increasing order of their bond strengths ?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "HMdDi",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{O}_2^{-} < \\mathrm{O}_2 < \\mathrm{O}_2^{+} < \\mathrm{O}_2^{2-}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "w14Dh",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{O}_2^{2-} < \\mathrm{O}_2^{-} < \\mathrm{O}_2 < \\mathrm{O}_2^{+}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "9xdF6",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{O}_2^{-} < \\mathrm{O}_2^{2-} < \\mathrm{O}_2 < \\mathrm{O}_2^{+}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "uu712",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{O}_2^{+} < \\mathrm{O}_2 < \\mathrm{O}_2^{-} < \\mathrm{O}_2^{2-}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "According to bond order values the given order is the answer. Bond order values are \n$+1,+1 \\frac{1}{2},+2$ and $+2 \\frac{1}{2}$, higher bond order means stronger bond.",
